Requirements: 33   with obligations: 32   deliberately none: 1

[task-01] Re-judge a criterion's test evidence only when something that criterion
    depends on has changed, and make a changed rating justify itself. A criterion
    depends on its requirement text, the set of tests mapped to it, and the contents of
    those tests. When a review repeated over stored earlier state finds all three
    unchanged, the stored rating stands and nothing is asked of the judge. When one of
    them did change, the judge is told what the rating was and what changed, and a
    rating it moves must rest on one of the changes it was given.
    -> rejudge-only-on-dependency-change  [functional/explicit]
       Re-judge a criterion's test evidence only when one of its dependencies changes,
       and keep the stored rating when the requirement text, mapped test set, and mapped
       test contents are all unchanged.
    -> dependency-change-justifies-rating-change  [invariant/explicit]
       A rating change made by the judge rests on one of the dependency changes it was
       given.

[constraint-01] A criterion whose requirement text, mapped test set and mapped test
    contents are all unchanged keeps the rating stored for it.
    -> unchanged-dependencies-keep-stored-rating  [invariant/explicit]
       A criterion whose requirement text, mapped test set and mapped test contents are
       all unchanged keeps the rating stored for it.

[constraint-02] Such a criterion costs no evidence-judgement model call.
    -> unchanged-dependencies-no-judge-call  [functional/explicit]
       Such a criterion costs no evidence-judgement model call.

[constraint-03] A criterion whose mapped test set gained or lost a member is judged
    again.
    -> mapped-test-set-changes-trigger-rejudge  [functional/explicit]
       A criterion whose mapped test set gained or lost a member is judged again.

[constraint-04] A criterion the contents of whose mapped tests changed is judged again.
    -> mapped-test-content-changes-trigger-rejudge  [functional/explicit]
       A criterion the contents of whose mapped tests changed is judged again.

[constraint-05] A criterion is compared against the stored state by the contents of its
    mapped tests, not by whether a file containing one of them was touched.
    -> compare-by-test-contents-not-file-touch  [compatibility/explicit]
       A criterion is compared against the stored state by the contents of its mapped
       tests, not by whether a file containing one of them was touched.

[constraint-06] Adding a test that is not mapped to a criterion does not cause that
    criterion to be judged again.
    -> unmapped-test-addition-does-not-rejudge  [regression/explicit]
       Adding a test that is not mapped to a criterion does not cause that criterion to
       be judged again.

[constraint-07] Editing a test mapped to one criterion does not change the rating of a
    criterion that test is not mapped to.
    -> editing-mapped-test-leaves-other-ratings-unchanged  [regression/explicit]   (also serves completion-04)
       Editing a test mapped to one criterion leaves every other criterion's rating
       unchanged.

[constraint-08] A judgement asked for a criterion that changed is given the rating
    stored for that criterion.
    -> changed-criterion-gets-stored-rating  [functional/explicit]
       A judgement requested for a changed criterion includes the stored rating for that
       criterion.

[constraint-09] A judgement asked for a criterion that changed is given the changes to
    that criterion's dependencies.
    -> changed-criterion-gets-dependency-changes  [functional/explicit]
       A judgement requested for a changed criterion includes the changes to that
       criterion's dependencies.

[constraint-10] The stored rating and the dependency changes given to a judgement are
    part of the request that judgement is recorded under.
    -> stored-rating-and-changes-recorded-with-judgement-request  [invariant/explicit]
       The stored rating and the dependency changes supplied to a judgement are recorded
       as part of the request under which that judgement is recorded.

[constraint-11] A judgement that alters a rating names one of the changes it was given.
    -> rating-change-must-name-given-change  [functional/explicit]
       A judgement that alters a rating names one of the changes it was given.

[constraint-12] A judgement that alters a rating while naming no change it was given is
    rejected by the code that reads the judgement, rather than by the instruction that
    asked for it.
    -> reject-judgement-without-named-change-in-reader  [error_handling/explicit]
       The code that reads a judgement rejects a rating change when the judgement names
       no change it was given.

[constraint-13] A rejected judgement leaves the stored rating in place.
    -> rejected-judgement-keeps-stored-rating  [invariant/explicit]
       A rejected judgement leaves the stored rating in place.

[constraint-14] A rejected judgement is reported.
    -> rejected-judgement-is-reported  [explanation_observability/explicit]
       A rejected judgement is reported.

[constraint-15] A review with no stored earlier state judges every criterion without
    reference to any stored rating.
    -> no-stored-state-judges-every-criterion  [functional/explicit]
       A review with no stored earlier state judges every criterion without reference to
       any stored rating.

[constraint-16] A review repeated over the same stored state and the same inputs
    produces the same review state as the one before it.
    -> byte-identical-review-state  [regression/explicit]   (also serves completion-09)
       Two reviews over the same stored state and the same inputs produce byte-identical
       review state.

[exclusion-01] Partitioning the evidence-judgement request so that one criterion's
